{"name":"Crowcore","title":"Crowcore","revision":231484,"url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Crowcore","retrieved":"2026-09-06","license":"CC BY-SA","licenseUrl":"https://www.fandom.com/licensing","language":"en","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Crowcore is sometimes used as an alternative to Goblincore, which has been criticized as anti-Semitic, but which shares the value of collecting small, lost, broken, thrown away, or conventionally trivial objects, and nature visuals."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"There is significant Tumblr cross-tagging between Crowcore, Gremlincore, Cottagecore, Cottagegore, and various other related aesthetics."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Visuals"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Some of these can include:"},{"kind":"list","text":"Old coins"},{"kind":"list","text":"Feathers"},{"kind":"list","text":"Tiny glittery pebbles/stones"},{"kind":"list","text":"Bones/Animal skulls(see Vulture Culture)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Rusty bottle caps"},{"kind":"list","text":"Tiny sculptures (usually of birds or other forest friends)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Vintage brooches/lockets"},{"kind":"list","text":"Seaglass"},{"kind":"list","text":"Items with crows present on them"},{"kind":"list","text":"Tincture bottles"},{"kind":"list","text":"Agates"},{"kind":"list","text":"Shiny sharp things like swords, knives, or daggers"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Activities"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Activities include (but are not limited to):"},{"kind":"list","text":"Sewing"},{"kind":"list","text":"Dressmaking"},{"kind":"list","text":"Collecting"},{"kind":"list","text":"Wading in creeks looking for frogs or salamanders"},{"kind":"list","text":"Organize your collections (putting them in pretty containers)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Reading"},{"kind":"list","text":"Studying"},{"kind":"list","text":"Feeding birds"},{"kind":"list","text":"Making charcoal drawings"},{"kind":"list","text":"Exploring"},{"kind":"list","text":"Spending time with friends"},{"kind":"list","text":"Playing D&D"},{"kind":"list","text":"Bird watching"},{"kind":"list","text":"Thrifting"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Books"},{"kind":"list","text":"A Wrinkle in Time by Madeline L’Engle"},{"kind":"list","text":"And Then There Were None by Agatha Christie"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Fashion"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Crowcore fashion is similar to Cottagegore and Goblincore. It is darker than Cottagecore but with light, mysterious, and playful aspects."}],"contentStatus":"full-source","images":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/3/30/Crowcore.PNG/revision/latest?cb=20200521150232","caption":"Crowcore · Visual reference 01","source":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/File:Crowcore.PNG","remote":true,"local":"images/detail/0236-1.webp","localAvailable":true},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/e/ed/Shinies.PNG/revision/latest?cb=20200521144817","caption":"Crowcore · Visual reference 02","source":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/File:Shinies.PNG","remote":true,"local":"images/detail/0236-2.webp","localAvailable":true}]}